cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "OptiFine: Energy-Aware Code Generation for AVR"
abstract: >-
  A research compiler backend that generates energy-aware AVR code for the
  ATmega128. It compiles an INT8 neural-network classifier from ONNX and a
  64-point Q15 DSP pipeline, prices every instruction with a cycle-exact
  energy model, and evaluates active-mode optimization and periodic
  Power-save scheduling in the Avrora simulator. All energy figures are
  simulated.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Partha Pratim
    family-names: Gogoi
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: https://github.com/rugbedbugg/OptiFine-AVR
license: MIT
keywords:
  - energy-aware compilation
  - AVR
  - ATmega128
  - embedded systems
  - TinyML
  - digital signal processing
  - Avrora
